Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; Remaps Caps Lock to F13 at the OS scancode level. Result: pressing the Caps
; Lock key no longer toggles upper/lower case — it sends F13 instead. WoW (and
; other apps) can bind to F13 like any other key.
;
; F13 exists in the USB HID keyboard spec but isn't physically on most modern
; keyboards, so remapping to it conflicts with nothing.
;
; HOW TO APPLY:
;   1. Double-click this file.
;   2. Click "Yes" to UAC prompt and "Yes" to the Registry Editor dialog.
;   3. Reboot Windows. The change requires a fresh boot.
;
; HOW TO REVERT:
;   Open Registry Editor (regedit), navigate to:
;     HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Keyboard Layout
;   Delete the "Scancode Map" value. Reboot.
;
; SCANCODE MAP DECODED:
;   header (8 bytes zero) + entry count (2 = mapping + terminator) +
;   target scancode (0x64 0x00 = F13) + source scancode (0x3A 0x00 = Caps Lock) +
;   null terminator (4 bytes zero)

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Keyboard Layout]
"Scancode Map"=hex:00,00,00,00,00,00,00,00,02,00,00,00,64,00,3A,00,00,00,00,00
